From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:50:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] meson: the objects of the library wait for the headers the
 build copies

src/libbluray/meson.build copies the API headers (bluray.h,
player_settings.h, ...) into the build folder with fs.copyfile(), so
that the library can be used as a subproject; libbluray_dep waits for
them, the library's own objects did not. A source in a subfolder of
src/libbluray that includes "bluray.h" (decoders/textst_render.c,
bdj/native/org_videolan_Libbluray.c, the remote/ files of the BD-J
host, and bluray.c through remote/bdr_client.h) does not find it beside
itself and finds the copy first (-Isrc/libbluray of the build folder
comes before the source tree's). With ninja running the copy and such a
compile at once, the compile could read a copy that was being written:

  src/libbluray/bluray.h:379:1: error: unterminated comment

The copies are now sources of the library, so that ninja makes them
before any of its objects. Nothing that is built changes.

Checked: in the build folder of meson 1.10, every one of the 62 objects
of the library has the eight copies among its order-only dependencies
(before: none), and a dry run of ninja for bluray.c.o and
textst_render.c.o from nothing copies bluray.h before the compile
(before: not at all); the library builds and its tests pass.
---
 src/meson.build | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index 7ace7e1..aa878d6 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -123,6 +123,8 @@ endif
 
 # The final libbluray library
 libbluray = library('bluray', libbluray_src,
+    # (the headers the build copies, before any object of the library: src/libbluray/meson.build)
+    libbluray_internal_headers,
     include_directories: libbluray_inc_dirs,
     dependencies: [
         fontconfig_dependency,
